---
import ConverterPage from '../components/ConverterPage.astro';
---

<ConverterPage
  path="/punjabi-font-converter"
  lede="Planned: a Punjabi font converter for AnmolLipi, Asees and other legacy Gurmukhi fonts to Unicode."
>
  <h2>Planned, not started</h2>
  <p>
    AnmolLipi and Asees are the legacy Gurmukhi fonts behind most older Punjabi
    documents. As with Kruti Dev, the text inside the file is ASCII and only
    becomes Punjabi when the right font is installed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Gurmukhi is a separate script from Devanagari with its own letters, vowel
    signs and subjoined forms, so nothing in the current engine transfers. The
    route exists so the work has a home; it will be switched on only after a
    keyword check and a mapping built from real AnmolLipi and Asees documents.
  </p>
</ConverterPage>
